    { q: 'Why do windows in east Ventura spot so badly after the sprinklers run?', a: "Because of the water, not the glass. Ventura uses only local water, and the groundwater part of it, from the Mound, Oxnard Plain, and Santa Paula basins, carries 1,200 to 1,600 mg/L of total dissolved solids before the city blends it, according to the city's 2024 drought resiliency grant application. East-end Santa Paula Basin water averages about 1,300 mg/L. When overspray dries on a window, those minerals stay behind as white spots. We rinse with purified water at 5 to 10 ppm so nothing is left to dry on the glass. Turning sprinkler heads away from the windows is the cheapest fix between cleanings." },
